summary:
- topic: Board Reconstitution & Communications
  text: The Board welcomed new member Adrian Dowling and held a land acknowledgement.
    The Chair introduced a new "Board Communications" agenda item, which members used
    to share positive updates from school visits and commendations for student activities
    like the high school band concert and robotics club. (Board Perspective)
- topic: Student Recognitions
  text: The Superintendent and Board honored students who earned All-State Music honors
    and recognized senior student-athletes named to the SMAA All-Academic and All-Citizenship
    teams, celebrating their achievements both in and out of the classroom. (Administration/Board
    Perspective)
- topic: 'District Reports: Student Data & Federal Funds'
  text: The administration reported a nearly 3% district-wide improvement in chronic
    student absenteeism compared to the previous year, attributing the success to
    a combination of broad communication and individualized family support. The Superintendent
    also proudly announced that the district had successfully expended every penny
    of its federal ESSER relief funds. (Administration Perspective)
- topic: Adult Education Program Update
  text: The Director of Adult Education presented on the program's rapid growth, particularly
    in ESOL services, and its new Integrated Education and Training (IET) program.
    She highlighted a significant funding challenge, noting the program is nearly
    70% reliant on unstable grants, and signaled a need for increased local investment
    in the upcoming budget to ensure sustainability. (Administration Perspective)
- topic: K-4 Math Curriculum Proposal
  text: The Director of Curriculum presented the recommendation to adopt the 'Into
    Math' program for grades K-4, replacing the 20-year-old 'Investigations' curriculum.
    The recommendation followed a thorough review process by a committee of educators,
    and the Board discussed the transition for teachers and families, particularly
    multilingual learners. The Board will vote on the quarter-million-dollar adoption
    in January. (Administration/Teacher/Board Perspective)
- topic: Mental & Behavioral Health Initiatives
  text: The new Director of Mental and Behavioral Health provided an update on the
    department's focus on suicide prevention, intervention, and postvention in response
    to recent community tragedies. She outlined partnerships with national and local
    organizations and announced a grant application with SoPo Unite for opioid settlement
    funds to enhance mental health services. (Administration Perspective)
- topic: 'Public Comment: Athletic Fields'
  text: A citizen representing a group of doctors, teachers, and environmental advocates
    spoke during the open audience of citizens. She urged the board to consider natural
    grass solutions over artificial turf for the high school athletic fields, citing
    health and environmental research, and requested a seat at the table for future
    discussions. (Citizen Perspective)
